# _matrix rules: code-reading notes

First, note the temporary objects at the top of the file. In `src/three/plugins/images/ImageOverlayPlugin.js`, line 21 is `_matrix`, followed immediately by `_vec`, `_center`, `_sphereCenter`, `_normal`, `_box`, and `SPLIT_TILE_DATA`. Searching only for `_matrix` on the first pass breaks this group of declarations apart.

The first four entries have been confirmed:

```js
const _matrix = /* @__PURE__ */ new Matrix4();
const _vec = /* @__PURE__ */ new Vector3();
const _center = /* @__PURE__ */ new Vector3();
const _sphereCenter = /* @__PURE__ */ new Vector3();
```

Lines 25 through 27 should still be noted alongside this group of locations: `_normal`, `_box`, `SPLIT_TILE_DATA`. The top of the file also imports `PriorityQueue`, the authentication plugin, and `XYZImageSource`; these won't be included in the matrix notes this time. Their actual roles remain to be filled in based on where each name appears.

# PLUGIN_REGISTERED Entry Point Notes

First, note `src/core/renderer/tiles/TilesRendererBase.js` as the starting point in this search for PLUGIN_REGISTERED. The earlier assessment was that reading registration-related code should start from this file, rather than working backward from an individual overlay call site. At the time, that assessment was only a working hypothesis to guide navigation.

The file header first shows four neighboring items:

```js
